## Why torch.while_loop Is Not Limited To Decode Here

For the earlier KV-blocking implementation, `torch.while_loop` was limited to the
Dynamo decode KV-blocking path because that loop iterates over KV cache blocks.
The initial production target was a fixed-CL decode ONNX model, so the static
maximum trip count is naturally `num_kv_blocks`. Prefill KV blocking has a
larger surface area: query blocking, causal masks, possible nested q/kv loops,
and more dynamic shape/mask cases. It can be implemented later, but it is not the
same loop as the decode KV-block loop.

For Qwen3.5 gated delta recurrence, the loop is different. It is a recurrence
over sequence tokens in `QEffQwen3_5GatedDeltaNet`, and it is enabled whenever
Dynamo is compiling that function. Therefore it can apply to prefill too. In
prefill, the Loop iterates over the prefill sequence length. In decode, it
usually iterates over one token. The gating condition is Dynamo compilation, not
`prefill_only`.

